{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Implemented + verified (2026-08-20) — three-layer prune safety, updater RE-ENABLED\n\nLanded host-local in `~/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh` (backup: `rebar-dev-update.sh.pre-df15`).\nNo repository code impact; git-ignored doc added at `docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md`.\n\n**Mechanism (as planned):**\n1. Bounded retention — `prune_releases()` never deletes `current`'s target nor the newest\n   RELEASES_KEEP=3 releases.\n2. flock liveness pinning — `~/.local/bin/rebar` and `rebar-mcp` are now generated wrapper\n   shims that take a SHARED non-blocking flock on `<release>/.inuse` and hold it across\n   `exec` for the process lifetime; the pruner takes an EXCLUSIVE non-blocking flock before\n   deleting (refused ⇒ live ⇒ kept). Verified flock survives exec on this host.\n3. Cap + alert — above RELEASES_CAP=10 retained (live-locked overflow), publish to SNS\n   `arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:896586841071:rebar-gerrit-alerts` (email→operator), throttled 1/24h;\n   never silently deletes a live release nor grows unbounded. Also alerts after 3 consecutive\n   candidate rejections (the b477339a99 43-run silent-pin class).\n\n**AC evidence:**\n- [x] Updater RE-ENABLED + running: `launchctl bootstrap` + `list` shows\n      `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update` (pid live); forced `launchctl kickstart -k` completed\n      exit 0. A by-hand run built origin/main `6e282021`, swapped `current`, installed shims,\n      pruned safely (`prune summary: pruned=0 kept-live=0 remaining=2`). Host no longer\n      drifting from origin/main.\n- [x] Long op spans an updater cycle: a long-lived global `rebar-mcp` (started through the\n      shim) pinned its release via flock and survived 3 forced update cycles; 12 continuous\n      global-shim `rebar list` calls across 3 forced cycles → 0 failures; pinned release\n      intact throughout.\n- [x] Bounded disk: oracle seeded 12 dead releases, KEEP=3 → reclaimed to 4 (current + newest\n      3), no alert. Bound stated: CAP=10 × ~346 MB ≈ 3.5 GB.\n- [x] Conflict ⇒ explicit ALERT not silent: oracle seeded 13 flock-held releases > CAP=10 →\n      `release-cap` alert published (captured via REBAR_DEV_ALERT_CMD seam) AND every live\n      release survived; negative control (same count unlocked) → pruned to 2, no alert.\n- [x] Documented in `docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md` (git-ignored): mechanism, N/M\n      rationale, tunables, pause/resume, alerting, rollback, and the restart-MCP-after-resume\n      note.\n- [x] Failure signature recorded (in that doc): ImportError naming a module that exists in the\n      tree with a now-missing `~/.local/state/rebar-dev/releases/` path ⇒ pruned-mid-run, not a\n      packaging defect.\n\n**Test rigor:** real-process/real-flock/real-prune oracles (not mocked); defect-seeded\nmutation (restoring the original unconditional `rm`) reproduces the exact DATA LOSS of a\nlive-locked release, confirming the oracle distinguishes fixed from broken. SNS publish access\nfrom this host verified live (MessageId bdc90c6e-...).\n\n**Transition note during rollout:** MCP servers started before the shim swap hold no flock and\nare covered only by layer-1 retention (~3 cycles); the doc instructs restarting them so they\npin via the shim."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787240726059542001,"uuid":"4dc06aeb-19d7-4dd0-aa1b-2bd2fb3895b0"}